WEBVTT

NOTE English visual guide. Editorial descriptions of on-screen concepts; no spoken narration.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
A complete language model connects the components built in the preceding lessons.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.400
Token IDs select token embeddings, which are combined with position embeddings.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.800
The resulting sequence passes through stacked Transformer blocks and a final normalization.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.600
A linear output head produces 65 logits for each position in the character vocabulary.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.800
Count parameters in embeddings, attention, feed-forward layers, normalization and the output head.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.600
The reference untied model has 162,561 parameters.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.400
Weight tying reuses the token embedding weights for the output projection. The shown tied

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.800
configuration has 158,401 parameters; the difference is 4,160.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Before training, compare the loss with ln(65), approximately 4.174, the uniform-prediction baseline.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Random logits need not give exactly uniform probabilities.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.800
Try to overfit one small batch. A large drop in that batch’s loss indicates that the model and

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.600
update path can learn those examples.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.400
Poor loss on a fresh batch after memorizing one batch demonstrates why training fit alone is

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.800
insufficient.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.600
In an encoder–decoder model, cross-attention takes queries from the decoder and keys and values from

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:55.200
the encoder output.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.800
The decoder’s causal self-attention and its cross-attention serve different purposes: reading its

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:07.600
own history and consulting the encoded input.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:18.000
Pause: what determines the number of logits per position? What does the one-batch test establish?

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.200
The vocabulary determines the number of logits. One-batch fitting is a debugging check, not evidence

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:34.400
of good performance on unseen data.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.070
Recap the complete model and its sanity checks before training on the text corpus.
